WEBVTT

00:00:25.049 --> 00:00:26.092
Oh.

00:00:26.843 --> 00:00:27.844
Where's the Professor?

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:29.429
Eh, probably dead.

00:00:29.512 --> 00:00:32.182
Already dissolving in a bathtub,
if we're lucky.

00:00:32.473 --> 00:00:34.225
I was out on the widow's walk

00:00:34.309 --> 00:00:38.646
keeping a hopeless vigil
for the return of my first delivery crew.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:41.816
It's been 50 years since they disappeared.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:43.818
Huh. I knew you had other crews,

00:00:43.902 --> 00:00:45.904
but you never told us
you had a first crew.

00:00:45.987 --> 00:00:48.823
I remember it like it was interesting.

00:00:50.158 --> 00:00:52.702
I had just built my new shipping
and receiving emporium.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:56.748
And I scoured
the hardware storeparking lot

00:00:56.831 --> 00:00:59.626
to assemble the finest crew imaginable.

00:00:59.709 --> 00:01:03.505
There was Candy,
the raunchy, by-the-books navigator,

00:01:03.588 --> 00:01:07.091
Lifter, the devastatingly
handsome forklift,

00:01:07.175 --> 00:01:12.680
and Captain Lando Tucker, a dedicated
young man with no characteristics.

00:01:12.764 --> 00:01:15.141
We'll deliver that package or die trying.

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:18.686
Hey, it's all my favorite patients.

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:21.981
And also Captain Tucker. Pow!

00:01:22.065 --> 00:01:23.399
Whoa!

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:26.653
You totally got me, Dr. John.
You're hilarious.

00:01:26.736 --> 00:01:28.446
Zoidberg was popular?

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:30.073
Zoidberg had hair?

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:32.200
I never said he had hair!

00:01:32.283 --> 00:01:35.453
If you chose to imagine him that way,
that's your business.

00:01:35.537 --> 00:01:39.332
Anyway, the time came
for our first delivery.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.670
Lando, don't forget about me and Junior.

00:01:43.753 --> 00:01:46.256
I won't, honey. Or die trying.

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:48.216
Well, crew, this is it.

00:01:48.299 --> 00:01:51.052
That cookie bouquet
isn't going to deliver itself.

00:01:53.263 --> 00:01:56.307
Ten, nine, and so on...

00:01:56.766 --> 00:01:57.767
Three,

00:01:58.268 --> 00:01:59.269
two,

00:01:59.811 --> 00:02:00.812
one...

00:02:05.984 --> 00:02:08.570
Go, you big metal bird. Get up there.

00:02:19.289 --> 00:02:20.790
Incredible!

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:22.500
Zoidberg had friends?

00:02:22.584 --> 00:02:24.002
It was a different time.

00:02:24.085 --> 00:02:25.920
Everything was going smoothly

00:02:26.004 --> 00:02:29.132
until right after that part
I was just telling you about.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:32.010
Suddenly, Amanda's aunt called to say

00:02:32.093 --> 00:02:34.971
her niece hadn't received
her cookie bouquet.

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:44.814
I watched the skies for weeks,

00:02:44.898 --> 00:02:48.693
with only occasional breaks
to tend to my grief diarrhea.

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.196
Just when all hope was lost...

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:55.408
The ship's escape pod!

00:02:59.037 --> 00:03:00.371
What happened up there, Johnny?

00:03:00.455 --> 00:03:04.209
Don't make me remember.
So horrible it was.

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:08.296
I thought you said he didn't have hair.

00:03:08.379 --> 00:03:13.134
Yes, but something he saw on that mission
traumatized him so severely,

00:03:13.218 --> 00:03:16.054
he grew hair, just so it could turn white.

00:03:16.137 --> 00:03:20.016
Sadly, my brave crew was gone forever.

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:26.147
That poor incompetent crew.

00:03:26.231 --> 00:03:28.149
What do you think happened, Professor?

00:03:28.816 --> 00:03:31.778
They were lost in the Bermuda Tetrahedron.

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:36.616
That's ridiculous.
The Bermuda Tetrahedron is just a myth.

00:03:36.699 --> 00:03:40.495
I'm glad you're so brave
in the face of the unknown, Leela,

00:03:40.578 --> 00:03:42.163
because, for your next mission,

00:03:42.247 --> 00:03:46.543
you'll be flying directly through
the Bermuda Tetrahedron!

00:03:48.086 --> 00:03:49.796
Or we could fly around it.

00:03:49.879 --> 00:03:52.757
Of course you could.
You'd be stupid not to.

00:03:52.841 --> 00:03:56.427
Supposing we're not stupid,
what kind of stupid mission is this?

00:03:56.511 --> 00:04:00.515
You'll be picking up a monument
commemorating my lost crew,

00:04:00.598 --> 00:04:04.143
to be unveiled Tuesday
at their memorial ceremony.

00:04:04.227 --> 00:04:06.855
All the grieving families will be there,

00:04:06.938 --> 00:04:08.481
plus a Popsicle cart.

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:12.569
You can count on us, Professor.
We'll get that monument here in time...

00:04:14.028 --> 00:04:15.113
...or die trying.

00:04:15.196 --> 00:04:16.573
What?

00:04:30.253 --> 00:04:34.424
Here you go. "In memory of the first
Planet Express ship and its crew."

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:37.218
Hang on.
"It's" shouldn't have an apostrophe.

00:04:37.302 --> 00:04:39.554
This means "and it is crew."

00:04:39.637 --> 00:04:40.930
What the hell's wrong with you?

00:04:41.014 --> 00:04:42.682
It's a minor error, lady.

00:04:42.765 --> 00:04:46.352
I mean, we're space aliens.
It's a miracle we can even speak English.

00:04:46.436 --> 00:04:48.605
The miracle is that
I'm not kicking your ass.

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:52.025
I insist you re-carve
the entire statue correctly.

00:04:52.108 --> 00:04:53.693
Okay, okay.

00:04:54.068 --> 00:04:56.988
Hey, Charlie,
hack off another block of ivory!

00:05:04.996 --> 00:05:07.081
Well, the statue's perfect now.

00:05:07.165 --> 00:05:10.168
Too bad we won't make it back
in time for the memorial service.

00:05:10.251 --> 00:05:12.587
We'll make it. Or die trying.

00:05:14.422 --> 00:05:16.925
We're cutting through
the Bermuda Tetrahedron!

00:05:17.008 --> 00:05:18.051
Whoo-hoo!

00:05:18.134 --> 00:05:20.637
Wait, the Bermuda Tetrahedron?

00:05:28.102 --> 00:05:31.439
I think I'm remembering
that thing I forgot.

00:05:32.315 --> 00:05:35.276
Uh-oh. The dials are terrified.

00:05:36.653 --> 00:05:39.572
Brace yourselves.
It's Tickle Me Elmo's Fire.

00:05:46.746 --> 00:05:49.290
There. See? It was no big thing.

00:05:50.625 --> 00:05:51.918
What was that big thing?

00:05:58.258 --> 00:05:59.884
It's a spaceship graveyard.

00:06:00.218 --> 00:06:02.262
Why did we have to come here at night?

00:06:02.345 --> 00:06:04.556
Look at all these famous lost ships.

00:06:04.639 --> 00:06:07.642
There's the Garmin!
And the TomTom!

00:06:07.725 --> 00:06:11.062
Over there!
It's the original Planet Express ship!

00:06:11.145 --> 00:06:14.983
What caused all that damage?
Could it have been flavor-blasted?

00:06:15.066 --> 00:06:16.484
We'd better investigate.

00:06:16.568 --> 00:06:19.946
Looks like an ion storm, though.
Everyone, suit up!

00:06:24.659 --> 00:06:27.620
Whatever happened here,
that first crew left in a hurry.

00:06:27.704 --> 00:06:30.415
The table is still set
for a McDonald's Value Dinner.

00:06:30.498 --> 00:06:32.417
I remember. I remember!

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:37.297
This is what traumatized me.
Such a meal to go to waste!

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:43.511
And with that, I have closure.

00:06:44.846 --> 00:06:47.265
Hey, Zoidberg, you're cockatieling.

00:06:47.348 --> 00:06:50.768
Oh, no. Something's happening.
What's happening?

00:06:57.358 --> 00:07:01.029
Oh, right.
And there was a giant killer space whale.

00:07:08.077 --> 00:07:11.122
Holy crap, it's a giant space fish!

00:07:11.206 --> 00:07:14.250
Actually, the space whale
isn't a space fish.

00:07:14.334 --> 00:07:15.710
It's a space mammal.

00:07:15.793 --> 00:07:18.963
Wow, interesting.
I'm both impressed and being eaten.

00:07:20.715 --> 00:07:23.885
Spacewalk, people!
Spacewalk for your lives!

00:07:27.138 --> 00:07:30.517
Man, look at him go.
Like a millionaire on a cocktail wiener.

00:07:50.912 --> 00:07:52.914
I did it. I outran him.

00:07:52.997 --> 00:07:54.874
Relax, friends.

00:07:58.711 --> 00:07:59.921
Panic, jerks!

00:08:00.004 --> 00:08:04.968
That's no ordinary space whale!
It's a four-dimensional space whale!

00:08:05.051 --> 00:08:06.094
Of course!

00:08:06.177 --> 00:08:10.849
And it only breaches into our 3-D universe
to hunt and fill its lungs with vacuum.

00:08:10.932 --> 00:08:15.603
Whatever its beef is, our one mission now
is to get that monument to Earth.

00:08:18.857 --> 00:08:23.153
Our one mission now
is to avenge the loss of that monument.

00:08:30.743 --> 00:08:33.288
Shmeesh! He gonked off the engines.

00:08:33.371 --> 00:08:34.372
That won't stop me.

00:08:34.455 --> 00:08:38.376
Raise the solar sails!
I'm going after that Möbius Dick!

00:08:40.378 --> 00:08:42.213
You've been hitting the Red Stripe, woman!

00:08:42.297 --> 00:08:44.382
Comport yourself, Mr. Conrad!

00:08:44.465 --> 00:08:47.427
When we're at space,
the captain's word is law.

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:50.680
I could marry you and Bender
against your will, if I wanted to.

00:08:50.763 --> 00:08:52.932
You wouldn't dare!

00:08:53.016 --> 00:08:54.392
I've been married to worse.

00:08:54.475 --> 00:08:58.897
Leela, I'm no doctor, but I'm afraid
you be exhibiting symptoms of illin'.

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:02.275
You're risking all our lives
for your own personal obsession.

00:09:02.358 --> 00:09:06.988
There's nothing personal about this.
That thing screwed up my delivery!

00:09:07.071 --> 00:09:09.532
This time, it's business.

00:09:44.567 --> 00:09:48.571
Maybe if I move the compass like this,
it will somehow kill the whale.

00:09:50.156 --> 00:09:52.033
Leela, we need to talk.

00:09:52.116 --> 00:09:55.870
You've gone from crazy like a fox
to crazy like Fox News.

00:09:55.954 --> 00:09:57.914
Fear not the space behemoth.

00:09:57.997 --> 00:10:03.461
In my dreams, I've peered beyond its eyes
and into the cackling hell within us all.

00:10:04.212 --> 00:10:06.089
Okay, that's a good point.

00:10:06.172 --> 00:10:09.092
Fry's right. Let's kill the captain
and order some strippers!

00:10:09.175 --> 00:10:10.593
Yeah, what he said.

00:10:10.677 --> 00:10:12.262
It's a mutiny led by Fry!

00:10:12.345 --> 00:10:15.014
That's enough insubordination, Mr. Fry!

00:10:15.098 --> 00:10:16.349
String him up!

00:10:28.486 --> 00:10:31.072
Things look bad enough
without having to look closer at them.

00:10:36.161 --> 00:10:37.787
Look, off in the distance!

00:10:38.079 --> 00:10:39.581
It's exhaling!

00:10:39.664 --> 00:10:41.249
Use boaty talk!

00:10:41.332 --> 00:10:44.335
Thar she blows!

00:10:46.713 --> 00:10:49.924
All right, which of you space dogs
has the guts and know-how

00:10:50.008 --> 00:10:51.259
to harpoon that whale?

00:10:51.342 --> 00:10:54.220
I spent a semester in Africa
harpooning giraffes.

00:10:54.304 --> 00:10:57.307
And giraffes are basically
just land space-whales.

00:10:57.390 --> 00:10:59.100
Ms. Wong, you have the 'poon.

00:11:13.281 --> 00:11:16.284
Oh, God, I'm having a Serengeti flashback.

00:11:16.743 --> 00:11:18.703
Die, you dirty giraffe!

00:11:24.209 --> 00:11:26.503
Well, I got it. Now what, Captain?

00:11:26.586 --> 00:11:28.129
You know, I'm not sure.

00:11:28.213 --> 00:11:30.548
I guess I thought whales died
when you harpooned them.

00:11:40.975 --> 00:11:43.144
Don't worry. I'll drop the anchor.

00:11:43.228 --> 00:11:44.938
Ouch!

00:11:46.981 --> 00:11:49.150
She's diving into the fourth dimension!

00:11:49.234 --> 00:11:50.735
We have to cut the rope!

00:11:50.819 --> 00:11:54.155
Negative, Sailor Moon.
We're going for a sleigh ride.

00:12:00.703 --> 00:12:02.872
I can see sideways in time.

00:12:05.291 --> 00:12:07.794
Gee, I see CGI.

00:12:10.338 --> 00:12:11.756
Poop.

00:12:12.048 --> 00:12:13.049
Poop.

00:12:13.132 --> 00:12:14.133
Aw, yeah.

00:12:14.217 --> 00:12:17.720
Bender, Bender, Bender
Bender, Bender, Bender

00:12:17.804 --> 00:12:21.349
Bender, Bender, Bender
Bender, Bender, Bender

00:12:27.397 --> 00:12:31.901
Aw! That was the greatest, unaccountably
infinite bunch of guys I ever met.

00:12:31.985 --> 00:12:35.655
Look out! It's pulling us
through a field of spacebergs.

00:12:37.657 --> 00:12:39.868
Stupid rocks. Think they're so great.

00:12:39.951 --> 00:12:42.120
Well, they are giant diamonds.

00:12:43.371 --> 00:12:45.623
Come to Papa.

00:12:47.709 --> 00:12:49.752
A lot of Bender
fell out of the crow's nest.

00:12:49.836 --> 00:12:51.045
We need to cut the line.

00:12:51.129 --> 00:12:53.715
Enough of your mad obsession
with Bender, Fry.

00:12:53.798 --> 00:12:56.467
We've got to murder that whale,
or die trying.

00:12:56.551 --> 00:12:58.219
This has gone too far.

00:12:58.303 --> 00:13:01.598
Bender's one of Planet Express's
most expensive appliances.

00:13:01.681 --> 00:13:02.765
And he's in trouble.

00:13:02.849 --> 00:13:04.684
That's it. I warned you.

00:13:04.767 --> 00:13:08.438
Fry, Zoidberg,
I now pronounce you man and...

00:13:09.606 --> 00:13:12.233
Oh, so close.

00:13:23.953 --> 00:13:27.749
Unsit me, Mr. Conrad.
We can't let the whale win.

00:13:30.752 --> 00:13:33.338
You're all too weak. I can see that now.

00:13:33.421 --> 00:13:37.133
So I'll have to be my own crew.
Understood?

00:13:37.217 --> 00:13:38.384
You've gone mad, Captain.

00:13:38.468 --> 00:13:39.677
That's enough out of me.

00:13:39.761 --> 00:13:42.180
Now, come on, I got to find that whale.

00:13:45.266 --> 00:13:46.434
I found him!

00:13:50.730 --> 00:13:54.317
With my Oxo Good Grips Cheese Knife,
I stab at thee.

00:13:58.655 --> 00:14:00.615
You do know I'm stabbing at thee, right?

00:14:32.605 --> 00:14:33.606
Hello.

00:14:35.233 --> 00:14:38.111
Think, Zoidberg.
You must remember something.

00:14:38.194 --> 00:14:39.237
No, nothing.

00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:41.239
For all I know,
our friends could have been eaten

00:14:41.322 --> 00:14:43.408
by some kind of crazy space whale.

00:14:43.491 --> 00:14:45.368
Damn that Bermuda Tetrahedron!

00:14:45.451 --> 00:14:49.581
It's taken my latest crew
just as it took my first one.

00:14:49.664 --> 00:14:52.667
Not to mention those single socks
from the dryer, am I right?

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:54.043
Shut up, Zoidberg.

00:14:54.335 --> 00:14:58.381
Oh, Zoidberg, the grieving relatives
will be gathered here tomorrow

00:14:58.464 --> 00:14:59.591
in need of comfort.

00:14:59.674 --> 00:15:01.593
And with no stone monument,

00:15:01.676 --> 00:15:05.054
they may well demand
that I refund their admission fees.

00:15:10.602 --> 00:15:12.353
Where are we?

00:15:12.437 --> 00:15:14.105
In the belly of the beast.

00:15:14.189 --> 00:15:16.608
Like that Bible guy
who got swallowed by the whale,

00:15:16.691 --> 00:15:17.692
Pinocchio.

00:15:17.775 --> 00:15:20.320
This is all Obsessy Bessy's fault.

00:15:20.403 --> 00:15:21.654
Right on, sister.

00:15:21.738 --> 00:15:23.948
We should be back at Planet Express
right now,

00:15:24.032 --> 00:15:25.783
hiding from work in the ceiling.

00:15:25.867 --> 00:15:27.327
But no!

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:29.829
For the last time, I'm not obsessed.

00:15:29.913 --> 00:15:33.166
I just want this whale to die, die, die!

00:15:35.919 --> 00:15:38.421
Uh-oh. What's that loud digesting sound?

00:15:42.717 --> 00:15:45.470
Holy crap! Four-dimensional bowels!

00:15:45.553 --> 00:15:46.888
Einstein was right.

00:15:56.356 --> 00:15:58.274
Why? Why?

00:15:58.358 --> 00:16:00.485
Also, what, and how?

00:16:00.568 --> 00:16:03.530
The great fish has chosen you
for a higher purpose.

00:16:03.613 --> 00:16:06.825
It's a great mammal.
See? It's got whiskers.

00:16:06.908 --> 00:16:08.785
And I saw it lactating earlier.

00:16:09.118 --> 00:16:10.453
Wait, who said that?

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:16.376
I was once Lando Tucker,
captain of the first Planet Express ship.

00:16:16.459 --> 00:16:17.627
Ew!

00:16:17.710 --> 00:16:21.381
I'm Turanga Leela, captain of
the current Planet Express ship.

00:16:21.464 --> 00:16:22.465
What's going on?

00:16:22.549 --> 00:16:23.550
It's very simple.

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:27.971
Well, actually it's very complicated.
Luckily, I'm here to explain it.

00:16:28.054 --> 00:16:32.141
You see,
this space whale feeds on obsession.

00:16:32.225 --> 00:16:35.353
Wow, are you gross looking! Go on.

00:16:35.436 --> 00:16:37.105
- The great space serpent...
- Mammal.

00:16:37.188 --> 00:16:40.817
...figured out long ago that no one's
more obsessed than space captains.

00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:46.072
What are these things? Get away!

00:16:46.156 --> 00:16:48.199
The whale's nearly sucked me dry.

00:16:48.283 --> 00:16:50.702
It'll need a new source of obsession
once I'm gone.

00:16:50.785 --> 00:16:53.621
How many times
do I have to tell other people?

00:16:53.705 --> 00:16:55.456
I'm not obsessed!

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:57.542
The whale is obsession, Leela.

00:16:57.625 --> 00:16:59.294
And you are the whale!

00:16:59.377 --> 00:17:01.171
I am not the whale!

00:17:01.254 --> 00:17:04.090
All I wanted was to complete my delivery.

00:17:04.174 --> 00:17:07.719
Is that too much to ask?
One chicken pickin' delivery?

00:17:07.802 --> 00:17:09.220
This whale's gonna pay.

00:17:09.304 --> 00:17:12.432
It can't escape what it already is, me!

00:17:12.515 --> 00:17:13.933
I am the whale!

00:17:16.227 --> 00:17:17.228
See?

00:17:31.701 --> 00:17:37.957
Fifty years, Junior.
Fifty years of crippling sorrow.

00:17:38.041 --> 00:17:41.294
Popsicles here.
Can't mourn the dead without a Popsicle.

00:17:41.377 --> 00:17:43.588
You think a Popsicle
gonna bring my daughter back?

00:17:43.671 --> 00:17:44.672
No, sir.

00:17:44.756 --> 00:17:47.342
Ha-ha! You just talked yourself
out of a sale.

00:17:48.843 --> 00:17:50.345
Poor Amy.

00:17:50.803 --> 00:17:53.598
My days of joy and luck are over.

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:55.725
Guess I got to quit that club.

00:17:55.808 --> 00:17:57.769
I can't believe our Leela's gone.

00:17:57.852 --> 00:18:01.940
You always think you're gonna
disappear in space before your children.

00:18:02.023 --> 00:18:03.650
Welcome, everyone.

00:18:03.733 --> 00:18:07.070
What a pleasure to see
so many miserable faces.

00:18:07.779 --> 00:18:09.948
Mmm! Lemony!

00:18:10.031 --> 00:18:14.452
I had intended to unveil
a beautiful stone memorial today.

00:18:14.536 --> 00:18:16.371
But due to the recent tragedy,

00:18:16.454 --> 00:18:19.916
I humbly ask you
to join me in a simple prayer.

00:18:22.377 --> 00:18:24.963
No refunds! Shut up and bow your heads!

00:18:25.463 --> 00:18:27.340
O, mighty Isis...

00:18:28.132 --> 00:18:30.593
Oh, no. My deal is doing the thing.

00:18:35.098 --> 00:18:38.977
Good Lord, it's some kind of
inter-dimensional space whale.

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:41.396
I just remembered, that's the guy.

00:18:42.647 --> 00:18:44.983
Oy! Now with the horror hair.

00:19:06.713 --> 00:19:10.091
Popsicles. Fill your gaping mouth
with a Popsicle.

00:19:12.468 --> 00:19:14.262
Leela, you're alive!

00:19:14.762 --> 00:19:17.056
Is that how
you and your friends are dressing now?

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:18.349
Hello, everyone.

00:19:18.433 --> 00:19:20.894
I suppose you're wondering
why my flesh has melded

00:19:20.977 --> 00:19:22.729
with that of a giant space whale.

00:19:22.812 --> 00:19:25.231
I'll admit to a polite interest.

00:19:25.315 --> 00:19:29.152
At first, I was consumed
by a dark obsession to kill the whale.

00:19:29.235 --> 00:19:31.029
Then I was consumed by the whale.

00:19:31.112 --> 00:19:33.823
That sounds clever,
but it doesn't explain much.

00:19:33.907 --> 00:19:35.950
-Shut up, Zoidberg.
-Okay.

00:19:36.034 --> 00:19:39.913
You see, beneath my obsession
lay an even deeper obsession.

00:19:39.996 --> 00:19:44.334
An obsession so strong, it allowed me
to overpower the beast's will

00:19:44.417 --> 00:19:46.503
and pilot it through space and time.

00:19:46.878 --> 00:19:50.048
An obsession with
completing my delivery.

00:19:54.719 --> 00:19:56.054
Get your...

00:19:58.431 --> 00:20:02.852
Poor Lando.
This is just how I want to remember him.

00:20:02.936 --> 00:20:05.438
Too bad, 'cause he's still alive.

00:20:07.690 --> 00:20:10.193
-Lando?
-Told you I'd be back.

00:20:10.276 --> 00:20:11.611
You've grown, Junior.

00:20:11.694 --> 00:20:13.112
I'm 61.

00:20:13.196 --> 00:20:15.114
I don't know him. What else you got?

00:20:27.669 --> 00:20:29.587
They haven't aged a day.

00:20:29.671 --> 00:20:32.507
The whale must have
some kind of Möbius colon

00:20:32.590 --> 00:20:35.176
that endlessly recycles time and space.

00:20:35.468 --> 00:20:37.637
Yep. That stands up to scrutiny.

00:20:39.013 --> 00:20:42.600
I should have listened to my crew.
That space whale wasn't a monster.

00:20:42.684 --> 00:20:45.061
It was the obsession
of me and others like me

00:20:45.144 --> 00:20:46.938
that made it into a monster.

00:20:47.230 --> 00:20:48.314
Mainly you.

00:20:49.357 --> 00:20:51.818
On the other hand,
the stupid fish did eat us.

00:20:51.901 --> 00:20:53.278
You guys want to do this?

00:20:53.361 --> 00:20:55.446
- Yeah.
- You know it!

00:20:57.073 --> 00:20:59.784
So, Johnny, are we gonna pick up
where we left off?

00:21:00.827 --> 00:21:01.828
Hey.